    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is a single acceptance test, and it passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `capacityWarning` \u2014 `true` when the owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners before this create (approaching the limit of 50). The hard rejection at 50 (`RejectCityAtCapacity` \u2192 409) is untouched.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **New function** `rest/function/owner/FlagCityCapacityWarning.java` \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (using the same trim/collapse-whitespace/lowercase normalization as `RejectCityAtCapacity`) and sets `capacityWarning = count >= 40 && count < 50`. It runs after `BuildOwner` (so the `Owner` and its city exist) and before `SaveOwner` (so `findAll()` excludes the new owner and the flag persists), mirroring the existing `FlagBulkSignup` pattern.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `flagCapacityWarning` step between `flagBulkSignup` and `detectPossibleDuplicate`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column field with getter/setter (mirrors `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to `OwnerDto`. The MapStruct mapper picks it up by name, so all `RespondWith*` paths (including the GET the test reads back) expose it.\n\n5. **Schema SQL** for all four DBs (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column. The hsqldb `data.sql` uses positional inserts, so I added a matching `NULL` per seed row (the others use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nThe value is persisted on the `Owner`, so it appears consistently on the create response and on subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 which is what the acceptance test asserts.",
